 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Email-as-Queue Workflow
     2	
     3	Issue: #2017
     4	
     5	Email is treated as a queue, not a durable archive. The durable record is the structured extraction written to the target repository; the raw email remains an operational input.
     6	
     7	## Scope
     8	
     9	#2017 defines the contract artifacts used by downstream implementation:
    10	
    11	- Local queue state model and schemas.
    12	- CRE extraction schema.
    13	- Spam classification rules.
    14	- Redacted fixture corpus and contract tests.
    15	
    16	Pipeline orchestration belongs to #2024. Queue-state storage implementation belongs to #2026. New Gmail-side delete/archive automation belongs to #2423.
    17	
    18	Existing `gmail-archive-extract.py` routing behavior is grandfathered production infrastructure. This design does not add new Gmail mutations.
    19	
    20	## Decisions
    21	
    22	### State Authority
    23	
    24	Queue state is local-only in v1:
    25	
    26	- Append-only event log: `scripts/email/queue-state.jsonl`.
    27	- Materialized read snapshot: `scripts/email/queue-state-snapshot.yaml`.
    28	- Snapshot freshness metadata: `scripts/email/queue-state-snapshot.meta.yaml`.
    29	- Learning/correction log: `scripts/email/queue-learning-log.jsonl`.
    30	
    31	Every thread identity is scoped by `(account_id, thread_id)`. Snapshot keys use `{account_id}::{thread_id}`.
    32	
    33	### Extraction Format
    34	
    35	Extracted records are YAML. CRE listings use `scripts/email/extraction-schemas/cre-listing-v1.yaml` and target `assethold/data/cre-listings`.
    36	
    37	### Deletion Safety
    38	
    39	`completed` threads are retained through a seven-day grace window. After the grace window, local queue state transitions to `purged`; Gmail content is not touched by this contract.
    40	
    41	### Reactivation
    42	
    43	Replies on `awaiting-reply`, `completed`, or `purged` threads transition back to `extracted` and link to the prior extraction when it exists. If a linked extraction is missing, the system emits `extraction_missing_on_reactivation` to both queue-state and learning logs, then treats the message as new inbound.
    44	
    45	### Learning Loop
    46	
    47	Manual corrections are appended to `queue-learning-log.jsonl`. Quarterly review reports summarize misclassifications, unknown senders, schema gaps, and spam false positives.
    48	
    49	### Spam Rules
    50	
    51	`scripts/email/spam-detection-rules.yaml` is evaluated before routing. Spam classification skips #2017 queue-state creation. If the sender is unmapped, the pipeline injects a synthetic `DELETE` routing action so the grandfathered routing path has an explicit action.
    52	
    53	## State Machine
    54	
    55	States: `inbound`, `extracted`, `awaiting-reply`, `completed`, `purged`.
    56	
    57	Transitions:
    58	
    59	- `inbound -> extracted`: actionable, data extraction, drive document, or archive classification.
    60	- `extracted -> awaiting-reply`: extracted data exists and a response is pending.
    61	- `extracted -> completed`: extracted data exists and no response is pending.
    62	- `awaiting-reply -> extracted`: new reply reactivates the topic.
    63	- `awaiting-reply -> completed`: user marks complete.
    64	- `completed -> purged`: seven-day grace has elapsed.
    65	- `completed -> extracted`: new reply reactivates the topic.
    66	- `purged -> extracted`: new reply reactivates with prior extraction context when available.
    67	
    68	Spam/noise/unsubscribe classifications may produce routing actions but do not create a #2017 queue-state entry.
    69	
    70	## Dependency Contract
    71	
    72	| Component | Owner |
    73	|---|---|
    74	| Design contract, schemas, fixtures, xfail contract tests | #2017 |
    75	| `scripts/email/queue_state.py` storage implementation | #2026 |
    76	| Pipeline orchestration and scheduled sweep wiring | #2024 |
    77	| Gmail-side delete/archive automation | #2423 |
    78	| Skill consolidation | #2019 |
    79	
