 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Email-as-Queue Workflow Design
     2	
     3	> **Issue:** [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017)
     4	> **Status:** Design specification
     5	> **Date:** 2026-04-09
     6	> **Supersedes:** Archive-everything approach in #1987, raw-email routing in gmail-archive-extract.py
     7	
     8	---
     9	
    10	## 1. Core Principle
    11	
    12	**Email is a queue, not an archive.**
    13	
    14	The previous system archived 36,100+ emails across 3 accounts into git repos by sender domain, storing full email bodies as markdown files. This created massive repo noise, inflated git history, and did not match how email should be managed.
    15	
    16	The new model treats every email as a transient item in a processing queue. Data enters the queue, gets triaged, has its actionable information extracted into structured form, and then the raw email is deleted. Only the extracted data persists in repositories.
    17	
    18	```
    19	                    +------------------+
    20	                    |    INBOUND       |
    21	                    |  (Gmail inbox)   |
    22	                    +--------+---------+
    23	                             |
    24	                    +--------v---------+
    25	                    |     TRIAGE       |
    26	                    | classify, route  |
    27	                    +---+----+----+----+
    28	                        |    |    |
    29	              +---------+    |    +----------+
    30	              |              |               |
    31	     +--------v---+  +------v------+  +-----v------+
    32	     |   NOISE    |  |   EXTRACT   |  |   REVIEW   |
    33	     | (delete)   |  | structured  |  | (hold for  |
    34	     +------+-----+  |   data      |  |  decision) |
    35	            |        +------+------+  +-----+------+
    36	            |               |               |
    37	            |        +------v------+        |
    38	            |        |     ACT     |        |
    39	            |        | commit data |        |
    40	            |        | to repos    |        |
    41	            |        +------+------+        |
    42	            |               |               |
    43	            |        +------v------+        |
    44	            |        | TRACK STATE |        |
    45	            |        | label thread|        |
    46	            |        +---+----+----+        |
    47	            |            |    |             |
    48	            |     +------+    +------+      |
    49	            |     |               |         |
    50	            | +---v--------+ +---v-------+  |
    51	            | | AWAITING   | | COMPLETED |  |
    52	            | | REPLY      | | (grace    |  |
    53	            | | (keep)     | |  period)  |  |
    54	            | +---+--------+ +---+-------+  |
    55	            |     |               |         |
    56	            |     | new reply     | 7 days  |
    57	            |     | arrives       | elapsed |
    58	            |     v               v         |
    59	            | RE-ACTIVATE     DELETE        |
    60	            |  (back to       (email gone,  |
    61	            |   INBOUND)       data stays)  |
    62	            +----+---+----+--------+--------+
    63	                     |
    64	              all deletions
    65	              logged locally
    66	```
    67	
    68	---
    69	
    70	## 2. Per-Account Rules
    71	
    72	### 2.1 ace (vamsee.achanta@aceengineer.com)
    73	
    74	| Category | Handling | Extraction Target |
    75	|---|---|---|
    76	| Active clients (RIL, DORIS, McDermott, Shell, etc.) | Extract project data, track threads | aceengineer-admin/data/client-{name}/ |
    77	| Recruiters (DISYS, Steps to Progress, etc.) | Extract role/rate/contact | aceengineer-admin/data/recruiting/ |
    78	| CRE listings (Sands IG, Marcus Millichap, LoopNet) | Extract property/cap-rate/tenant data | assethold/data/cre-listings/ |
    79	| Software vendors (ANSYS, DNV, ENGYS) | Extract license/support data only if actionable | aceengineer-admin/data/vendor/ |
    80	| Industry colleagues | Keep for networking touchbase, extract contact if new | aceengineer-admin/data/colleague/ |
    81	| Marketing/newsletters | DELETE immediately or after unsubscribe | -- |
    82	
    83	VIP domains requiring immediate attention: `ril.com`, `dorisgroup.com`, `mcdermott.com`, `shell.com`, `kbr.com`, `bp.com`, `subsea7.com`, `technipfmc.com`
    84	
    85	### 2.2 personal (achantav@gmail.com)
    86	
    87	| Category | Handling | Extraction Target |
    88	|---|---|---|
    89	| Family (achanta* gmail addresses) | Keep while active, extract key dates/actions | achantas-data/data/family/ |
    90	| Financial (banks, insurance, tax) | Extract amounts/dates/due-dates | achantas-data/data/finance/ |
    91	| Tax documents (TurboTax, 1099s, K-1s) | Extract form type/amounts/year | achantas-data/data/tax/ |
    92	| Alumni / career networking | Extract contact updates | achantas-data/data/networking/ |
    93	| Social media notifications | DELETE immediately | -- |
    94	| Marketing / promotions | DELETE after batch unsubscribe | -- |
    95	
    96	### 2.3 skestates (skestatesinc@gmail.com)
    97	
    98	| Category | Handling | Extraction Target |
    99	|---|---|---|
   100	| Tenant (Family Dollar, Dollar Tree) | Extract issue/resolution/dates | sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/tenant/ |
   101	| Insurance (Marsh, Crown Insurance, Insureon) | Extract policy/claim/premium data | sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/insurance/ |
