   106	
   107	VIP domains requiring immediate attention: `familydollar.com`, `dollartree.com`, `marsh.com`
   108	
   109	---
   110	
   111	## 3. Thread Lifecycle
   112	
   113	### 3.1 States
   114	
   115	| State | Gmail Label | Meaning | Auto-delete? |
   116	|---|---|---|---|
   117	| inbox | (none) | New, untriaged | No |
   118	| extracted | `wh-email/extracted` | Data pulled, no pending action | No |
   119	| awaiting-reply | `wh-email/awaiting-reply` | Operator replied, waiting for counterparty | Never |
   120	| completed | `wh-email/completed` | Topic resolved, grace clock starts | After 7 days |
   121	| noise | `wh-email/noise` | Spam/newsletter, no extraction needed | Immediately |
   122	
   123	### 3.2 Transition Rules
   124	
   125	```
   126	inbox -----------> extracted          (data successfully extracted and committed)
   127	inbox -----------> noise              (classified as spam/newsletter/promotion)
   128	inbox -----------> review             (system cannot classify; held for user)
   129	
   130	extracted -------> awaiting-reply     (operator sends a response in the thread)
   131	extracted -------> completed          (no reply needed; topic is resolved)
   132	
   133	awaiting-reply --> inbox              (new inbound reply arrives -- RE-ACTIVATE)
   134	awaiting-reply --> completed          (topic resolved without further reply)
   135	
   136	completed ------> inbox              (new inbound reply during grace period -- RE-ACTIVATE)
   137	completed ------> [DELETED]          (grace period elapsed, no new replies)
   138	
   139	noise ----------> [DELETED]          (immediate or batch delete)
   140	```
   141	
   142	### 3.3 Re-activation
   143	
   144	When a thread marked `completed` or `awaiting-reply` receives a new inbound message:
   145	
   146	1. Gmail automatically surfaces the thread in inbox (unread notification)
   147	2. The system detects the `wh-email/*` label on the thread plus the new unread message
   148	3. The existing label is removed and the thread returns to `inbox` state
   149	4. The local state log is updated with `reactivated_date` and `reactivation_count`
   150	5. Triage runs again on the thread
   151	
   152	### 3.4 Grace Period
   153	
   154	- Duration: 7 calendar days from `completed_date`
   155	- During grace period: thread stays in Gmail with `wh-email/completed` label
   156	- If new reply arrives: grace timer resets, thread returns to inbox
   157	- After grace period with no new reply: thread is deleted from Gmail
   158	- Local state log retains the deletion record permanently (for audit trail)
   159	
   160	---
   161	
   162	## 4. Data Extraction Targets
   163	
   164	### 4.1 What Gets Extracted (structured data only)
   165	
   166	| Email Type | Extracted Fields | Destination Repo/Path | Format |
   167	|---|---|---|---|
   168	| CRE listing | property_name, tenant, address, state, price, cap_rate, building_sf, lease_years, vpd, broker | assethold/data/cre-listings/ | YAML |
   169	| Client RFP/SOW | sender, company, project, scope_summary, timeline, budget, contacts | aceengineer-admin/data/prospects/ | YAML |
   170	| Invoice/payment | invoice_number, vendor, amount, due_date, status, payment_method | per-account finance path | YAML |
   171	| Tenant communication | store_number, issue_type, date_reported, resolution, vendor, cost_estimate | sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/tenant/ | YAML |
   172	| Tax document | form_type, entity, tax_year, amounts, due_date, filing_status | achantas-data/data/tax/ | YAML |
   173	| Recruiter outreach | company, role, rate, location, contact_name, contact_email | aceengineer-admin/data/recruiting/ | YAML |
   174	| Insurance | policy_number, carrier, premium, coverage_type, renewal_date, claim_number | sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/insurance/ | YAML |
   175	| New contact | name, email, company, category, source_thread | contact-manager pipeline | CSV row |
   176	
   177	### 4.2 Extraction Format
   178	
   179	All extracted data uses YAML as the canonical format:
   180	
   220	- Automated system notifications with no actionable content
   221	
   222	---
   223	
   224	## 5. State Tracking System
   225	
   226	### 5.1 Dual-Layer Tracking
   227	
   228	**Layer 1: Gmail Labels (operational visibility)**
   229	
   230	Gmail labels in the `wh-email/` namespace provide real-time visibility inside the Gmail UI and allow Gmail search queries for state-based filtering (e.g., `label:wh-email/completed older_than:7d`).
   231	
   232	Labels are created lazily via the Gmail API when first needed. Label operations use `users/me/threads/{id}/modify` to apply labels at the thread level.
   233	
   234	**Layer 2: Local State File (authoritative audit trail)**
   235	
   236	`~/.hermes/email-state.yaml` is the authoritative state tracker. It records every state transition, extraction event, and deletion. This file survives Gmail label drift and provides the data needed for the learning loop.
   237	
   238	```yaml
   239	# ~/.hermes/email-state.yaml
   240	threads:
   241	  - thread_id: "18f3a2b..."
   242	    account: ace
   243	    subject: "Dollar General NNN | TX | 7.25% CAP"
   244	    sender_domain: sandsig.com
   245	    state: completed
   246	    extracted_to: "assethold/data/cre-listings/"
   247	    extracted_date: "2026-04-07"
   248	    completed_date: "2026-04-08"
   249	    eligible_for_deletion: "2026-04-15"
   250	    last_activity: "2026-04-08"
   251	    reply_count: 0
   252	    reactivation_count: 0
   253	
   254	  - thread_id: "18f3a2c..."
   255	    account: skestates
   256	    subject: "Family Dollar Store #30150 HVAC Issue"
   257	    sender_domain: familydollar.com
   258	    state: awaiting-reply
   259	    extracted_to: "sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/tenant/"
   260	    extracted_date: "2026-04-05"
   261	    last_activity: "2026-04-07"
   262	    reply_count: 3
   263	    reactivation_count: 1
   264	
   265	deletions:
   266	  - thread_id: "18f3a1a..."
   267	    account: personal
   268	    deleted_date: "2026-04-08"
   269	    reason: "noise — marketing newsletter"
   270	    had_extraction: false
   271	
   272	  - thread_id: "18f3a2b..."
   273	    account: ace
   274	    deleted_date: "2026-04-15"
   275	    reason: "completed — grace period elapsed"
   276	    had_extraction: true
   277	    extracted_to: "assethold/data/cre-listings/"
   278	```
   279	
   280	### 5.2 State File Operations
   281	
   282	| Operation | Trigger | State File Update |
   283	|---|---|---|
   284	| New thread scanned | Triage run | Add entry with state=inbox |
   285	| Data extracted | Extraction pipeline | state -> extracted, set extracted_date and extracted_to |
   286	| Operator replied | Send/draft detection | state -> awaiting-reply |
   287	| Topic resolved | User marks complete | state -> completed, set completed_date and eligible_for_deletion |
   288	| New reply arrives | Unread scan on labeled thread | state -> inbox, increment reactivation_count |
   289	| Deleted | Deletion sweep | Move to deletions list, remove from threads list |
   290	
   291	---
   292	
   293	## 6. Routing Configuration Evolution
   294	
   295	### 6.1 Current State (archive-first)
   296	
   297	`scripts/email/email-routing.yaml` currently maps sender domains to raw archive paths:
   298	
   299	```yaml
   300	"familydollar.com": "sabithaandkrishnaestates/docs/email/tenant"
   301	"sandsig.com":      "assethold/data/sandsig-cre-listings/email"
   302	```
   303	
   304	### 6.2 Target State (queue-first)
   305	
   306	The routing file evolves to specify extraction templates and structured data destinations:
   307	
   308	```yaml
   309	rules:
   310	  # ---- NOISE (delete, no extraction) ----
   311	  "collide.io":                     { action: DELETE }
   312	  "promote.weebly.com":             { action: DELETE }
   313	
   314	  # ---- REVIEW (hold for user decision) ----
   315	  "substack.com":                   { action: REVIEW }
   316	
   317	  # ---- EXTRACT (structured data extraction) ----
   318	  "sandsig.com":
   319	    action: EXTRACT
   320	    template: cre-listing
   321	    destination: assethold/data/cre-listings/
   322	    account: ace
   323	
   324	  "familydollar.com":
   325	    action: EXTRACT
   326	    template: tenant-communication
   327	    destination: sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/tenant/
   328	    account: skestates
   329	
   330	  "marsh.com":
   331	    action: EXTRACT
   332	    template: insurance
   333	    destination: sabithaandkrishnaestates/data/insurance/
   334	    account: skestates
   335	
   336	  # ---- DEFAULT ----
   337	  "default":
   338	    action: REVIEW
   339	    destination: achantas-data/data/unclassified/
   340	```
   341	
   342	### 6.3 Migration Path for Routing
   343	
   344	1. Keep current `email-routing.yaml` working during transition (backward compatibility)
   345	2. Add a `routing-v2.yaml` with the new schema alongside the old file
   346	3. New extraction pipeline reads `routing-v2.yaml`; old script continues with current file
   347	4. After parity is confirmed, rename v2 to primary and deprecate old file
   348	
   349	---
   350	
   351	## 7. Technical Implementation
   352	
   353	### 7.1 Tools and APIs
   354	
   355	| Component | Tool | Notes |
   356	|---|---|---|
   357	| Email reading | Gmail REST API (urllib, no pip deps) | Direct OAuth2 with refresh tokens |
   358	| Email CLI fallback | himalaya v1.2.0 | For IMAP operations where API is overkill |
   359	| Token management | `~/.gmail-{ace,personal,skestates}/credentials.json` | Auto-refresh via refresh_token grant |
   360	| OAuth config | `~/.gmail-mcp/oauth-env.json` | Shared client_id / client_secret |
   361	| Triage scheduling | Hermes cron | Daily at 7 AM CT (triage), 12 PM CT (digest) |
   362	| Legal scanning | `scripts/legal/legal-sanity-scan.sh` | Runs before every git commit of extracted data |
   363	| Contact enrichment | `scripts/email/contact-normalizer.py` outputs | CSV lookup during triage classification |
   364	| State persistence | `~/.hermes/email-state.yaml` | Local YAML, not in git |
   365	
   366	### 7.2 Scripts (new and modified)
   367	
   368	| Script | Purpose | Status |
   369	|---|---|---|
   370	| `scripts/email/gmail-extract-and-act.py` | Queue-first extraction pipeline | NEW (replaces gmail-archive-extract.py) |
   371	| `scripts/email/templates/*.yaml` | Per-domain/type extraction field definitions | NEW |
   372	| `scripts/email/gmail-digest.py` | Daily digest, updated to be state-aware | MODIFY |
   373	| `scripts/email/email-routing.yaml` | Current routing file | KEEP (backward compat) |
   374	| `scripts/email/routing-v2.yaml` | New queue-aware routing schema | NEW |
   375	| `scripts/email/gmail-archive-extract.py` | Archive-first extraction | DEPRECATE after parity |
   376	
   377	### 7.3 Gmail Label Management
   378	
   379	Labels are managed via the Gmail API:
   380	
   381	```
   382	POST /gmail/v1/users/me/labels       -- create wh-email/* labels (lazy, first use)
   383	POST /gmail/v1/users/me/threads/{id}/modify  -- add/remove labels on threads
   384	GET  /gmail/v1/users/me/messages?q=label:wh-email/completed+older_than:7d  -- find deletion candidates
   385	```
   386	
   387	The `wh-email/` prefix namespaces all automation labels to avoid collisions with user labels.
   388	
   389	### 7.4 Extraction Pipeline Pseudocode
   390	
   391	```
   392	function run_extraction(account, query, dry_run):
   393	    token = refresh_oauth_token(account)
   394	    routing = load_routing_v2()
   395	    state = load_state_file()
   396	
   397	    messages = gmail_search(token, query)
   398	
   399	    for each message in messages:
   400	        domain = extract_sender_domain(message)
   401	        rule = routing.lookup(domain)
   402	
   403	        if rule.action == DELETE:
   404	            if not dry_run: gmail_trash(message)
   405	            log_deletion(state, message, reason="noise")
   406	            continue
   407	
   408	        if rule.action == REVIEW:
   409	            log_review_needed(state, message)
   410	            continue
   411	
   412	        if rule.action == EXTRACT:
   413	            template = load_template(rule.template)
   414	            fields = template.parse(message.subject, message.body, message.attachments)
   415	
   416	            if not fields.validates():
   417	                log_extraction_failure(state, message, reason="insufficient fields")
   418	                continue
   419	
   420	            yaml_output = format_yaml(fields)
   421	            legal_ok = legal_scan(yaml_output)
   422	
   423	            if not legal_ok:
   424	                log_legal_block(state, message)
   425	                continue
   426	
   427	            if not dry_run:
   428	                write_yaml(rule.destination, yaml_output)
   429	                git_commit(rule.destination_repo, f"extract: {domain} data")
   430	                label_thread(message.thread_id, "extracted", token)
   431	
   432	            update_state(state, message, new_state="extracted")
   433	
   434	    save_state_file(state)
   435	    return stats
   436	```
   437	
   438	### 7.5 Deletion Sweep Pseudocode
   439	
   440	```
   441	function run_deletion_sweep(account, dry_run):
   442	    token = refresh_oauth_token(account)
   443	    state = load_state_file()
   444	
   445	    for each thread in state.threads:
   446	        if thread.account != account:
   447	            continue
   448	
   449	        if thread.state == "noise":
   450	            if not dry_run: gmail_delete(thread.thread_id, token)
   451	            move_to_deletions(state, thread, reason="noise")
   452	
   453	        if thread.state == "completed":
   454	            if days_since(thread.completed_date) >= 7:
   455	                # Check for new replies before deleting
   456	                has_new = check_for_new_messages(thread.thread_id, token)
   457	                if has_new:
   458	                    reactivate(state, thread)
   459	                    continue
   460	                if not dry_run: gmail_delete(thread.thread_id, token)
   461	                move_to_deletions(state, thread, reason="grace period elapsed")
   462	
   463	        if thread.state == "awaiting-reply":
   464	            # NEVER auto-delete
   465	            pass
   466	
   467	    save_state_file(state)
   468	```
   469	
   470	---
