   542	## 10. Migration Plan
   543	
   544	### 10.1 From Archive-Everything to Queue Model
   545	
   546	| Step | Action | Risk | Mitigation |
   547	|---|---|---|---|
   548	| 1 | Create `routing-v2.yaml` alongside existing routing file | None | Old file still works |
   549	| 2 | Build `gmail-extract-and-act.py` with dry-run mode | None | No side effects in dry-run |
   550	| 3 | Create first 5 extraction templates (CRE, client, tenant, tax, invoice) | Low | Templates are additive |
   551	| 4 | Run extraction pipeline in dry-run on all 3 accounts | None | Validates templates against real data |
   552	| 5 | Enable extraction (write YAML to repos) with `wh-email/extracted` labels | Low | Data is additive, no deletions yet |
   553	| 6 | Enable noise deletion (known spam domains only) | Low | Already identified in current routing |
   554	| 7 | Enable completed+grace-period deletion on ace account | Medium | 7-day grace + trash (not permanent delete) |
   555	| 8 | Extend deletion to personal and skestates | Medium | Same safeguards |
   556	| 9 | Deprecate `gmail-archive-extract.py` | Low | New pipeline has parity |
   557	| 10 | Retire deprecated active skills (gmail-extract-and-clean, gmail-extract-archive, gmail-email-to-repo-extraction, gmail-touchbase, gmail-unsubscribe) | Low | Active folders removed; archived twins retained under `.claude/skills/email/_archived/` |
   558	
   559	### 10.2 Existing Data
   560	
   561	Raw email archives already committed to repos are not deleted retroactively. They remain in git history. Going forward, no new raw email bodies are written to repos. Only structured YAML extractions are committed.
   562	
